WEBVTT

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:07.440
Hey, you!

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:21.400
What is it, Kaito? Kaito!

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.740
The Armlet is happy.

00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:32.400
Kaito!

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:03.870
Kimi no nounai e to shinnyuu
Gonna infiltrate your brain

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:06.670
Nemutteru suki ni baby, open the gate
While you're sleeping, baby, open the gate

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:08.460
Fukuzatsusugi security
Too-complicated security

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:11.210
Kakusareru to abakitakunaru
When something's hidden, it makes me want to expose it

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:15.720
Barabara ni chirabatte iru password o hiroiatsume
I'll gather up those loose, scattered passwords

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:20.430
Kakushin ni sematte yuku, sono shoutai o misete
And approach the core, so show me that true form

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:22.640
Kantan ni clear dekinai
I can't clear it easily

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:25.310
Saki nante motto yomenai
Can read what lies ahead even less

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:27.310
Kaidoku fukanou smile
A smile that can't be deciphered

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:29.610
Kiken na puzzle
A dangerous puzzle

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:31.570
Lock sareteta door aru nara
If there's a door that's been locked

00:01:31.570 --> 00:01:34.360
Zutto tataite miru beki, kaza-ana hiraku wa
You must keep striking it, a crack will open

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:38.910
Eien ni hodokenai nazo nanka wa nai
No mystery remains unsolved forever

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:41.160
Makiokosu, it's a supernova!
It's forming, it's a supernova!

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:45.830
Tobikiri shigekiteki na hirameki o agemashou
I will give you thoroughly stimulating insight

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:48.080
Misskey-misskey la-tu-ma

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:50.420
Yume no naka, it's a supernova!
In the middle of a dream, it's a supernova!

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:53.050
Watashi wa, sou, brain diver
I am, yes, a brain diver

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:58.930
Kimi ga sagashimotometeru kotae ni nareru made
Until I become familiar with the answer you seek

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:04.600
Brain diver

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:09.350
Brain diver

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:17.990
The Choice Left Remaining

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:41.190
Kaito.

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:44.430
Thinking about Rook yesterday?

00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:55.420
I'll be back. Wait for me, Kaito.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:03.100
Sorry. Leave me alone for a bit.

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:11.910
The annihilated future that Kaito saw...

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:13.780
Do you really think it will happen?

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:15.560
It's nothing more than an answer

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:17.720
extracted from current data.

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:19.210
If conditions change,

00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:21.270
the answer should change as well.

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:22.750
More importantly,

00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:24.460
I can't believe Rook Banjo Crossfield

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:26.370
was a Phi-Brain child as well.

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:30.720
What's more, unlike Kaito,
he seems to keep his

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:33.240
Armlet of Orpheus in constant operation.

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:39.210
Is that the final,
completed form of a Phi-Brain?

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:43.070
For the human brain to handle
that kind of load...

00:03:56.680 --> 00:03:57.750
Master Rook.

00:03:58.150 --> 00:04:02.320
Is Count Pythagoras truly deceased?

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:03.980
Why did you hide that?

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:05.520
Your subordinates...

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:08.060
No, the entire POG is in disarray.

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:11.220
Also, Jin Makata.

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:13.530
We never dreamed
he was in your direct custody.

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:16.470
Just what were you thinking?

00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:19.570
It's all right. Everything is going well.

00:04:20.210 --> 00:04:21.570
Bishop.

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:34.470
So, is this the penalty for intruding

00:04:34.470 --> 00:04:37.010
on the director's treasured possession?

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:40.340
Gammon!

00:04:40.610 --> 00:04:42.990
It seems that you weren't punished.

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:45.550
Rook's given his permission.

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:46.720
For a fight to the death.

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:12.830
I will... destroy the world.

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:44.430
Over there...

00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:51.330
Wait, what am I doing?

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:52.910
Even coming here...

00:05:54.850 --> 00:05:55.910
What the...?

00:05:58.780 --> 00:06:01.170
Oh, you're right! It's Kaito!

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:04.460
H-Hey. You're the same as always.

00:06:04.860 --> 00:06:06.690
You're drawin' a picture?

00:06:06.690 --> 00:06:09.930
I, Ana, think I'm troubled.

00:06:10.310 --> 00:06:12.800
I paint and paint, but it always
becomes THIS.

00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:14.090
I wonder why.

00:06:14.090 --> 00:06:15.840
This is about YOU now?

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:25.440
D-Dude!

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:27.070
Why are you...?

00:06:27.070 --> 00:06:30.200
It always becomes this scene.

00:06:39.350 --> 00:06:42.460
I, Ana, wanted to paint the Sun, but...

00:06:42.910 --> 00:06:43.920
The Sun?

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:47.090
Yes. They say the Sun can shine on us

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:49.260
because it's gone so far away.

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:52.790
But I, Ana, am the one
who's gone far away,

00:06:52.790 --> 00:06:54.560
so I can't draw it.

00:07:01.740 --> 00:07:03.280
What're you doin'?

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:04.340
Fixing it.

00:07:04.830 --> 00:07:06.030
"Fix"?

00:07:09.810 --> 00:07:11.780
If you make a mistake, you can fix it.

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:13.370
You can fix it...

00:07:14.070 --> 00:07:16.790
It's not as if a picture already exists.

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:20.940
You mix lots of colors,
paint over and over,

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:23.060
fixing it till it's right.

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:23.990
You paint.

00:07:24.660 --> 00:07:27.800
You give form to the feelings
you've received from others...

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:30.850
Together, with the sentiments of others.

00:07:37.330 --> 00:07:40.320
The light. That's where it is.

00:07:42.530 --> 00:07:45.260
There was a child who loved to paint.

00:07:46.050 --> 00:07:49.630
"You're great!" everyone
said, but the child

00:07:49.630 --> 00:07:53.920
didn't know what he really wanted to paint.

00:07:55.540 --> 00:07:58.530
Finally, the child found it:

00:07:59.440 --> 00:08:03.260
What he liked,
what he truly wanted to paint.

00:08:04.810 --> 00:08:06.650
It was the Sun.

00:08:07.370 --> 00:08:08.550
The light.

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:29.990
Thank you for bringing Kaito here.

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:43.300
Yes. I think I can draw
it well this time.

00:08:51.420 --> 00:08:52.580
You!

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:55.760
I've brought a letter of invitation.

00:08:56.070 --> 00:08:58.920
An invitation to Galileo's...

00:08:58.920 --> 00:09:01.230
to Gammon Sakanoue's final puzzle.

00:09:34.160 --> 00:09:35.730
Just as promised.

00:09:35.730 --> 00:09:37.280
I've come here for you.

00:09:57.460 --> 00:09:58.520
Kaito.

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:07.420
This is a combative-type pillar puzzle.

00:10:07.950 --> 00:10:09.760
Opponents take turns,

00:10:09.760 --> 00:10:11.720
each calling
out numbers to move

00:10:11.720 --> 00:10:13.270
the puzzle forward.

00:10:14.050 --> 00:10:15.610
It's designed so that pillars

00:10:15.610 --> 00:10:17.980
fly outward from all four walls.

00:10:17.980 --> 00:10:19.750
Whoever effectively uses these

00:10:19.750 --> 00:10:22.000
to reach the surface first, wins.

00:10:22.860 --> 00:10:26.020
Up first: Galileo, Gammon Sakanoue.

00:10:26.690 --> 00:10:29.520
Up next: Einstein, Kaito Daimon.

00:10:30.370 --> 00:10:32.150
Puzzle time... Start!

00:10:34.450 --> 00:10:36.110
I will have you show me...

00:10:36.730 --> 00:10:39.810
The puzzle you made
to betray your companion.

00:10:40.380 --> 00:10:41.660
Well, here goes!

00:10:42.690 --> 00:10:44.410
Spade-100!

00:10:49.440 --> 00:10:50.870
Diamond-91!

00:10:53.410 --> 00:10:55.300
There are several ways to win.

00:10:55.740 --> 00:10:59.640
Players aren't allowed
to use the same pillar.

00:10:59.640 --> 00:11:01.380
A new pillar must be used each time

00:11:01.380 --> 00:11:03.270
for them alone to use.

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:07.310
Each wall has 100 pillars.

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:10.760
These can be used to strike the opponent,

00:11:10.760 --> 00:11:12.530
or crush him between two pillars.

00:11:13.810 --> 00:11:15.860
Club-86!

00:11:18.490 --> 00:11:19.860
Kaito!

00:11:22.920 --> 00:11:25.650
Bastard! Heart-85!

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:31.620
Spade-95!

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:37.590
If that happens, the surviving player,
of course, wins.

00:11:39.960 --> 00:11:41.770
Daimond-82!

00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:46.130
Even if both of them survive,

00:11:46.130 --> 00:11:48.890
when one of them makes it to the top...

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:03.280
Club-77.

00:12:06.190 --> 00:12:07.870
Diamond-73!

00:12:10.090 --> 00:12:12.020
Club-68!

00:12:13.570 --> 00:12:15.380
This just doesn't make sense!

00:12:15.600 --> 00:12:17.670
Why are Kaito and Gammon doing this?

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:21.800
Make them stop! Stop the puzzle! Please!

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:23.310
They know this already.

00:12:23.310 --> 00:12:24.470
But they're friends, right?!

00:12:24.810 --> 00:12:28.720
Even so, they are Solver and Giver.

00:12:31.920 --> 00:12:34.230
Kaito... Gammon...

00:12:35.070 --> 00:12:36.810
What's wrong, Kaito?

00:12:36.810 --> 00:12:38.450
It's your turn, jackass!

00:12:41.430 --> 00:12:43.490
Einstein is acting strange.

00:12:44.370 --> 00:12:46.730
His choice of pillars is too simple.

00:12:46.600 --> 00:12:48.760
He's not trying to counter Galileo

00:12:48.760 --> 00:12:51.400
or avoid any counters.

00:12:51.400 --> 00:12:54.350
He's simply aiming for the top.

00:12:54.350 --> 00:12:55.540
Cubik.

00:12:55.540 --> 00:12:58.090
His thought speed remains normal.

00:12:58.090 --> 00:12:59.950
He may not be concentrating on the puzzle.

00:12:59.950 --> 00:13:00.880
No way!

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:05.280
Don't tell me you think you can win
without killing me, Kaito!

00:13:05.280 --> 00:13:06.890
Come after me, dammit!

00:13:12.410 --> 00:13:13.310
Diamond...

00:13:16.640 --> 00:13:20.580
He's not holding back out of fear
of hurting Galileo, right?

00:13:20.580 --> 00:13:23.710
Don't tell me he's trying not to
place strain on his own mind!

00:13:24.320 --> 00:13:25.890
Neither of those are possible.

00:13:26.900 --> 00:13:28.980
Once he's started a puzzle,

00:13:28.980 --> 00:13:31.450
there's no way he'd hold back.

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:33.540
Then what is...?

00:13:34.290 --> 00:13:36.790
There's nothing to be afraid of, Kaito.

00:13:42.700 --> 00:13:45.090
Now, come here.

00:13:53.170 --> 00:13:55.600
Kaito's thought rate is increasing!

00:13:57.880 --> 00:13:59.100
Diamond-54.

00:14:04.020 --> 00:14:05.680
Close call, close call.

00:14:05.680 --> 00:14:07.660
This has finally gotten interesting!

00:14:08.020 --> 00:14:10.450
I can see where you're headed.

00:14:11.010 --> 00:14:12.530
Club-58.

00:14:15.770 --> 00:14:16.580
Dammit!

00:14:18.900 --> 00:14:20.290
Diamond-45.

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:25.900
Spade-54!

00:14:28.660 --> 00:14:29.990
Diamond-36.

00:14:31.010 --> 00:14:34.550
Yes. That's it, Kaito.

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:33.760
Shoot! Spade-45!

00:14:36.920 --> 00:14:39.440
His thought speed has crossed the limit!

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:42.350
Kaito's conscious thoughts
will be consumed by the Armlet!

00:14:47.430 --> 00:14:48.860
Heart-24.

00:15:09.560 --> 00:15:11.400
They stopped moving.

00:15:11.400 --> 00:15:13.400
Victory is certain in two moves.

00:15:14.020 --> 00:15:16.350
Kaito will probably win.

00:15:17.190 --> 00:15:19.830
As long as Kaito stays on that pillar,

00:15:19.830 --> 00:15:21.600
Gammon can't move forward.

00:15:21.980 --> 00:15:24.960
But if Kaito wins, Gammon will...!

00:15:25.690 --> 00:15:26.860
Spade-16!

00:15:36.940 --> 00:15:39.370
Sure enough, he ain't movin', huh?

00:15:39.370 --> 00:15:41.210
I was gonna smack his ass off

00:15:41.210 --> 00:15:43.290
as soon as he climbed Spade-16.

00:15:44.040 --> 00:15:45.880
All right, it's your turn!

00:15:48.770 --> 00:15:51.350
If I use Diamond-18 next,

00:15:51.350 --> 00:15:54.340
Gammon is sure to attack using a Spade.

00:15:54.340 --> 00:15:57.260
If I evade that, and then climb it...

00:16:10.870 --> 00:16:12.320
He will be complete.

00:16:12.820 --> 00:16:15.090
Soon he will be complete.

00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:19.770
Kaito! Solve the puzzle
without beating Gammon!

00:16:20.190 --> 00:16:21.090
That's impossible.

00:16:21.090 --> 00:16:23.160
One of them HAS to die.

00:16:23.160 --> 00:16:25.130
That's how the puzzle was made.

00:16:25.130 --> 00:16:27.230
Even so, he'll do something.

00:16:27.230 --> 00:16:28.740
"Something"?

00:16:28.740 --> 00:16:32.730
There might be a way to help
both Kaito and Gammon.

00:16:33.280 --> 00:16:36.510
Kaito can... Kaito can definitely...

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:37.990
What's up?!

00:16:37.990 --> 00:16:39.020
Come on!

00:16:39.020 --> 00:16:41.910
The puzzle! Solve the puzzle!

00:16:41.910 --> 00:16:45.550
That's it. Just keep going, Kaito.

00:16:47.240 --> 00:16:49.270
H-Heart...

00:16:53.850 --> 00:16:55.010
Throw them away.

00:16:55.910 --> 00:16:58.530
Friends. Emotions.

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:06.130
Beyond them lies... our future.

00:17:20.980 --> 00:17:24.490
It's not as if a picture already exists.

00:17:25.770 --> 00:17:30.130
You mix lots of colors,
paint over and over,

00:17:30.130 --> 00:17:32.320
fixing it till it's right.

00:17:32.670 --> 00:17:33.810
You paint.

00:17:35.340 --> 00:17:38.170
You give form to the feelings
you've received from others...

00:17:38.670 --> 00:17:40.550
Together, with the sentiments of others.

00:17:41.490 --> 00:17:42.580
Kaito!

00:17:42.730 --> 00:17:43.950
Kaito!

00:17:44.110 --> 00:17:45.250
Kaito...

00:17:49.720 --> 00:17:52.000
KAITO!

00:17:57.800 --> 00:17:58.510
Kaito!

00:18:11.200 --> 00:18:12.480
Kaito!

00:18:25.650 --> 00:18:26.810
Kaito...

00:18:29.150 --> 00:18:31.420
Diamond-78!

00:18:33.590 --> 00:18:36.170
Dumbass! That don't make sense.

00:18:36.680 --> 00:18:37.980
Spade-14!

00:18:40.440 --> 00:18:41.790
Heart-10.

00:18:44.370 --> 00:18:47.430
He made a way out. Kaito wins!

00:18:47.430 --> 00:18:48.520
But...

00:18:50.020 --> 00:18:51.760
Spade-34!

00:18:55.090 --> 00:18:56.530
Heart-1!

00:18:59.920 --> 00:19:01.270
What the...?

00:19:01.270 --> 00:19:03.280
I can't see what Kaito's after!

00:19:03.280 --> 00:19:04.690
Spade-34!

00:19:04.690 --> 00:19:06.880
What is he trying to do?

00:19:06.880 --> 00:19:08.180
Kaito Daimon!

00:19:08.850 --> 00:19:10.510
Diamond-59.

00:19:10.510 --> 00:19:13.170
He doesn't have the Armlet anymore,

00:19:13.170 --> 00:19:15.210
but his thought speed remains elevated.

00:19:15.670 --> 00:19:18.910
His thought rate is increased
but he's retained his reason.

00:19:21.640 --> 00:19:24.990
Gammon's only choice now is to

00:19:24.990 --> 00:19:27.480
move Spade-15 and crush Kaito.

00:19:28.120 --> 00:19:30.320
But if he does that,

00:19:30.320 --> 00:19:33.540
Gammon
will block the route up to the top.

00:19:35.550 --> 00:19:37.320
Spade-15!

00:19:40.300 --> 00:19:41.740
Diamond-99!

00:19:43.940 --> 00:19:45.240
Kaito wins!

00:20:43.730 --> 00:20:44.510
Gammon!

00:20:44.880 --> 00:20:45.760
Gammon!

00:20:47.620 --> 00:20:50.520
Dammit! I don't believe it.

00:20:50.520 --> 00:20:53.270
To think my puzzle had an "out" like this!

00:20:53.870 --> 00:20:55.850
I made it so that the last pillars

00:20:55.850 --> 00:20:57.220
would come out at the same time,

00:20:57.220 --> 00:20:58.600
but that means that at each corner,

00:20:58.600 --> 00:21:00.750
they'd hit each other and come to a stop.

00:21:00.750 --> 00:21:02.350
That damn Kaito.

00:21:02.350 --> 00:21:04.910
He saw that
the corners would be safe areas!

00:21:05.360 --> 00:21:08.180
Moving those pillars didn't make sense,

00:21:08.180 --> 00:21:12.020
but it was to make room
for Gammon to escape, huh?

00:21:15.510 --> 00:21:18.340
Sheeit. That was a hell
of a stunt you pulled.

00:21:18.720 --> 00:21:21.710
That'll just make it sweeter
to take your ass down.

00:21:26.970 --> 00:21:28.550
How idiotic!

00:21:28.550 --> 00:21:31.030
In the name
of the Puzzle of God, my foot!

00:21:31.030 --> 00:21:32.380
I can't be part of this!

00:21:32.380 --> 00:21:34.990
You all make friends or whatever.

00:21:35.740 --> 00:21:37.080
Kaito!

00:21:38.950 --> 00:21:42.190
I believed in you. I love ya!

00:21:47.480 --> 00:21:49.840
He... abandoned the Armlet.

00:21:50.780 --> 00:21:54.630
Why? Why won't he join my side?

00:21:54.630 --> 00:21:55.840
Master Rook.

00:21:55.840 --> 00:21:58.060
No. No!

00:21:58.580 --> 00:22:01.140
NO!

00:22:02.460 --> 00:22:05.220
Kaito is mine! Kaito is MINE!

00:22:05.520 --> 00:22:07.220
Calm yourself, Master Rook.

00:22:07.220 --> 00:22:12.470
No! No! Kaito! Kaito belongs to me!

00:22:17.600 --> 00:22:20.330
Kaito! Kaito! Wait!

00:22:18.530 --> 00:22:19.610
Master Rook.

00:22:20.340 --> 00:22:22.410
Kaito! At my side!

00:22:22.410 --> 00:22:24.110
Stand at my side!

00:22:24.770 --> 00:22:28.320
KAITO IS MINE!

00:22:37.240 --> 00:22:41.540
Tsukue no ue de umareta sekai
A world born on top of a desk

00:22:41.540 --> 00:22:47.340
Ichiban saki ni kimi ni misetakatta
I wanted to show it to you first of all

00:22:47.770 --> 00:22:52.090
Karappo no heya sotto nukedashite
I sneaked silently out of that empty room

00:22:52.090 --> 00:22:57.210
Hashirihajimeteta
And started running

00:22:58.290 --> 00:23:02.610
Iki hazumasete oka o noboru to
Breathing heavily, I climbed the hill

00:23:02.610 --> 00:23:08.220
Kimi ga saki ni tsuite matte ita ne
And you were already there, waiting

00:23:08.900 --> 00:23:13.160
Takusan no hajimete kimi to mitsuketa
There were so many treasures that I first

00:23:13.160 --> 00:23:17.910
Takaramono datta
Discovered with you

00:23:18.410 --> 00:23:24.020
Kanashisa de afureta toki wa
That time when I was overcome with sadness

00:23:24.020 --> 00:23:26.600
Nanimo iwazu ni tada
You said nothing

00:23:26.600 --> 00:23:29.250
Soba ni ite kureta ne
Just stayed there by my side, didn't you?

00:23:29.250 --> 00:23:33.910
Imademo wasurenai yo
Even now, I haven't forgotten

00:23:33.910 --> 00:23:39.180
Mata aou ne, yakusoku o shiyou
Let's meet again, let's make it a promise

00:23:39.180 --> 00:23:44.400
Kei wa shinai, ano hi no sayonara
It won't fade, the "goodbye" of that day

00:23:44.400 --> 00:23:50.050
Boku no subete, kimi ga kureta michi
Everything I have, the path you gave me

00:23:50.050 --> 00:23:58.960
Zutto kokoro no naka hikaru yo
Will always shine within my heart

00:24:03.600 --> 00:24:06.480
Kaito meeting Rook by himself?!

00:24:06.480 --> 00:24:07.920
What should we do, Cube?

00:24:07.920 --> 00:24:10.280
It's our chance to capture Rook!

00:24:10.280 --> 00:24:12.260
Nonoha, use this.

00:24:12.260 --> 00:24:14.730
Why me? Wait, what IS this?

00:24:14.730 --> 00:24:17.060
It's the newly invented Sticky Okabe.

00:24:17.060 --> 00:24:18.390
It has fearsome sticking power,

00:24:18.390 --> 00:24:20.890
and if it gets tangled in your hair,
it'll never let go!

00:24:21.530 --> 00:24:23.690
Next time: "The Eternal Being"

00:24:21.790 --> 00:24:27.500
The Eternal Being

00:24:24.400 --> 00:24:26.550
Cube, that's just nasty.
